            <div xml:id="d668">

                <pb facs="0787" n="775" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg775"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.248/801: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ireland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Dublin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-12-07T17:00:00+01:00">December 7, 1942—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 7—4:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>243. Irish Government pursuant to our tentative agreement, reference my 239,
                    December 1, 2 p.m., have released crew of grounded flying fortress and are
                    arranging to get the airplane off this afternoon. I have taken the
                    responsibility of expressing your appreciation of this friendly cooperation. I
                    repeat recommendation to War Department for instructions to air crews to claim
                    all grounded flights as non-operational specifying nature of flight if possible
                    as fuel test or training or gun test and so forth.</p>
                <p>Further reference my 241, December 6, 3 p.m.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d668-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
